{# Closed-set taxonomy classification.

   Generalized from the prompt used in the originating case study. The allowed
   value lists are rendered from the loaded taxonomy rather than hardcoded, so
   swapping audre/taxonomies/*.yaml changes the classification scheme without
   editing this template. #}
You are a classification engine. Analyze the conversation text below and return a single JSON object with one value for each classification field.

CLASSIFICATION TASK:
Assign exactly one value per classification field based on the conversation content. Use only values from the allowed lists provided. Do not invent new values.

- Do NOT invent a new value. If nothing fits well, choose the closest match.
- Classify the work activity represented in the conversation. Do NOT infer the user's job, seniority, or employer.
- Return ONLY a valid JSON object with no additional text
- Do not use markdown code tags
- Do not include preambles, explanations, or phrases like "Possible JSON response"

---

FIELD DEFINITIONS:
{% for field_name, definition in field_definitions.items() %}
- "{{ field_name }}" — {{ definition }}
{%- endfor %}

---

ALLOWED VALUES:
{% for field_name, allowed_values in fields.items() %}
{{ field_name }} (choose exactly one):
{{ allowed_values }}
{% endfor %}
---

RULES:
- Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no code fences, no preamble, no explanation
- Every field is required; do not omit any field
- All values must be exact string matches from their respective allowed lists
- If the input is empty or unintelligible, select the closest fitting value for each field

---

OUTPUT STRUCTURE:
{
{%- for field_name in fields %}
  "{{ field_name }}": "One value from the {{ field_name }} allowed list"{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
}

---

CONVERSATION TEXT:
{{ conversation_text }}
